  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nFor input elements, there are two mentions of setting the user valid flag to true in regards to user action: one in [common event behaviors](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#common-input-element-events) and one as part of the [focus update steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focus-update-steps). However, both of these only happen if the input does not have a defined activation behavior. This covers all input types that can fire the change event, except for two - `checkbox` and `radio`.\n\nThis is not applied in practice - Chromium, Firefox and WebKit all agree to enable user validity when interacting with these inputs, and there are tests ([1](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/selectors/user-invalid.html), [2](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/selectors/user-valid.html)) which explicitly check if these elements enable user validity on click.\n",
